evidence is overwhelmingly on my side? And so once you end up in a situation where the issue is important, we are interdependent in terms of our actions and beliefs, and both of us believe that there's more evidence on our side than the other side. Then it's very hard to just let the other person keep believing whatever it is they want to. And I'm thinking about you and your colleague Francis as you were sitting at your kitchen table arguing about the results of the paper. Uh-huh. You know, in some ways it meets all three criteria. It does. It's, you know, years of work and we're stuck together because we're co-authors and we both think we have the right answer.

